        "original_id": "11faefca-9c96-526d-beb5-cc838ada34b3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mariana Kovacevic, Asamoah Gyan\n- Roles: Serbian traditional healer, Ghanaian professional footballer, striker, captain\n- Concepts: Horse placenta treatment\n- Events: 2012 African Cup of Nations\n- Places: Gabon, Equatorial Guinea, Accra\n- Organizations: Ghana national team, Kayserispor\n\nFacts:\n- Asamoah Gyan was born on 22 November 1985 in Accra.\n- Mariana Kovacevic is a Serbian traditional healer who specializes in using horse placenta treatment to heal athletes.\n- During the 2012 African Cup of Nations in Gabon and Equatorial Guinea, Mariana Kovacevic used horse placenta treatment to heal Ghana's Asamoah Gyan after an injury that was expected to keep him out of football for four weeks.\n- Asamoah Gyan is a Ghanaian professional footballer who plays as a striker for Kayserispor and captains the Ghanaian national team.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
